    "digestRule": "keccak256(abi.encode(\"EnclaveStateRegistry.commitFor\", chainId, registry, enclave, keyHash, keccak256(bytes(cid)), expectedVersion, relayNonce, nonce)): EnclaveStateRegistry.commitDigest",
    "signatureRule": "EIP-191 personal_sign of the 32-byte digest (eth-account encode_defunct, ethers signMessage over the digest bytes) by the ESR wallet; commitFor recovers it and requires the signer to be the enclave; the trustedzone vets every record in an envelope against esr.wallet the same way before counting it",
    "callerRule": "callerUsed is the task caller the step ran under, which the trustedzone requires to equal the holder it attested; owned marks a commit to an owned key"
  },
  "envelope": {
    "layout": "{ack, code, data, commits, esr: {wallet, commits}}",
    "rules": [
      "ack, code and data as today: the input object number answered, the payload code, the payload output",
      "commits: the names of the step's session.commit.<n>.<key16>.<relayNonce>.json files, n the step's output object number, in key then relay-nonce order; an empty list for a step without commits",
      "esr.commits: the signed authorization records of those commits in the same order, the objects ecld_state appends to esr.authorizations.json; esr.wallet the securelock's ESR address; a session's ESR ledger is the concatenation of its steps' esr.commits in staging order, the bytes esr.authorizations.json holds",
      "the envelope is signed and encrypted for the trustedzone as every step output is; the trustedzone takes esr.commits as the ledger whichever way the session ends, so a transfer stop or a toBlock cut leaves it a ledger to sign the ESR fields over",
      "esr.authorizations.json on a session: the securelock rewrites it after each session.output.<n> envelope as the compact JSON array of every staged step's records in staging order (a step cut by transfer or never emitted contributes nothing); the trustedzone's session ledger is the concatenation of the records it took from the envelopes of the rows it staged, serialised compactly (JSON.stringify / json.dumps with separators (\",\", \":\")) with the record objects' nine keys in record order, exactly as esrCommitDigest hashes them, so the two are byte-equal; when the result envelope's esr.commits also exists the two must be equal, else SECURITY_VIOLATION; the agent pins the file as the attested ledger when its raw CIDv1 equals result field 6"
    ]
  },
